---
/**
 * What a caught mistake looks like: the list of jobs of the guards-first
 * workflow (ci/guard-first.yml in mainstay) and the output of a failing check,
 * verbatim from README.md. Heavy jobs need the guards, so they are skipped.
 *
 * The text inside the card stays in English in every language: it is what the
 * checks print. `live` plays the run once when the page opens.
 *
 * `fix` adds a switch under the card: the reader "fixes" the mistake and the
 * same run turns green, the heavy jobs run. It is a checkbox and CSS, so it
 * works without JavaScript.
 */
import { plugin } from "../data/case";
import { typo } from "../lib/site";

interface Props {
  caption: string;
  /** Show the list of jobs above the output. */
  jobs?: boolean;
  /** Play the run when the page opens. */
  live?: boolean;
  /** The switch: its two labels and the caption of the green run. */
  fix?: { run: string; back: string; caption: string };
}

const { caption, jobs = true, live = false, fix } = Astro.props;
const out = plugin.redOutput;
const red = [
  { state: "pass", mark: "✓", name: "Should CI run?", note: "" },
  { state: "fail", mark: "✕", name: "Guards", note: "1 violation" },
  { state: "skip", mark: "–", name: "Tests + build", note: "skipped" },
  { state: "skip", mark: "–", name: "Integration", note: "skipped" },
];
const green = red.map((check) => ({ ...check, state: "pass", mark: "✓", note: "" }));
const afterChecks = jobs ? red.length : 0;
---

<figure class="ci">
  {fix && <input class="ci__toggle visually-hidden" type="checkbox" id="ci-fix" />}
  <div class:list={["ci__card", live && "ci__card--live"]}>
    <div class="ci__run ci__run--red">
      <div class="ci__bar">
        <span>checks</span>
        <span class="ci__bar-status" style={`--i:${afterChecks + 1}`}>1 failing</span>
      </div>
      {
        jobs && (
          <ul class="ci__checks">
            {red.map((check, i) => (
              <li class={`ci__check ci__check--${check.state}`} style={`--i:${i}`}>
                <span class="ci__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                  {check.mark}
                </span>
                <span>{check.name}</span>
                <span>{check.note}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        )
      }
      <pre class="ci__output" style={`--i:${afterChecks}`}><code><span class="ci__title">{out.title}</span>{"\n\n"}  {out.file}  {out.rule}  {out.message}{"\n\n"}<span class="ci__hint">{out.hint}</span></code></pre>
    </div>
    {
      fix && (
        <div class="ci__run ci__run--green">
          <div class="ci__bar">
            <span>checks</span>
            <span class="ci__bar-status ci__bar-status--pass" style={`--i:${green.length + 1}`}>
              {green.length} passing
            </span>
          </div>
          <ul class="ci__checks">
            {green.map((check, i) => (
              <li class="ci__check ci__check--pass" style={`--i:${i}`}>
                <span class="ci__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                  {check.mark}
                </span>
                <span>{check.name}</span>
                <span />
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
          <p class="ci__passed" style={`--i:${green.length}`}>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="24" cy="24" r="21" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" />
              <path d="M14.5 24.5l6.5 6.5 12.5-13.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
            </svg>
            All checks have passed
          </p>
        </div>
      )
    }
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span class="ci__caption ci__caption--red">{typo(caption)}</span>
    {fix && <span class="ci__caption ci__caption--green">{typo(fix.caption)}</span>}
  </figcaption>
  {
    fix && (
      <label class="ci__fix" for="ci-fix">
        <span class="ci__fix-run">{fix.run}</span>
        <span class="ci__fix-back">{fix.back}</span>
      </label>
    )
  }
</figure>
